        "project_citation_role": "FLT software, ongoing Lean formalization, Kevin Buzzard and Richard Taylor, Imperial College London,2025. This project citation is separate from the exact three source bylines and is not acceptance of a complete FLT proof.",
        "selected_endpoint": {
          "declaration": "FreyCurve.j_valuation_of_bad_prime",
          "exact_statement": "lemma j_valuation_of_bad_prime (P : FreyPackage) {q : ℕ} (hqPrime : q.Prime)\n    (hqbad : (q : ℤ) ∣ P.a * P.b * P.c) (hqodd : 2 < q) :\n    (P.p : ℤ) ∣ padicValRat q P.freyCurve.j",
          "scope": "For P:FreyPackage,q:Nat, q prime, (q:Int) divides P.a*P.b*P.c and2<q, the conclusion is (P.p:Int) divides padicValRat q P.freyCurve.j. The valuation is Int-valued; the divisor is p, not q.",
          "source_doc_typo": "The module main-theorem overview says multiple of q, but the actual declaration and near-theorem docstring say p. Bind to the declaration.",
          "denominator_extension_boundary": "Any selected new denominator theorem must retain an explicit separate qden:q divides P.freyCurve.j.den premise if its proof uses it. Do not infer qden merely from the name bad_prime or silently derive it from hqbad; no such bridge has been supplied in this audit."
        },
        "stable_url": "https://github.com/ImperialCollegeLondon/FLT/blob/a3210204ad8876e851e32f73dd97d882bf1ccd0a/FLT/FreyCurve/Basic.lean"
